Z||000000||FieroLisa||02-24-2001||10:32 PM||||How the heck do you get the dash map pocket off? Someone please tell me it is possible without taking the entire dash apart. I got almost my entire interior painted, thanks to Roger Garrison's assistance in teaching me how to paint  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">, but can't finish the dash because I can't paint around that map pocket. I have a new one, so if I must rip the old one off I can- but I'd rather not.<P>Anyway today involved a long 6 hours amidst non-stop paint fumes...and driving home in the GT with practically no interior in it...good fun  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>Tarheels Fieros Website</A><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/pffsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||William||02-24-2001||11:03 PM||||Lisa,<BR>The dash must be removed to properly remove the pocket. It may be possible to rip the old pocket out and then using double sided tape to install the new one, but you will be risking damage that may not be hidden by the new pocket. You are painting your dash without removing it? Scary thought!<P>Just reread your post and I'm not sure if you did or didin't remove the dash. If the dash is out, you will now need to remove the air duct on the back to access the map pocket nuts.<p>[This message has been edited by William (edited 02-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroLisa||02-24-2001||11:07 PM||||William<BR>    Painting went quite well without removing dash- I took off the center console, pillars, everything except door panels and the dash (but took all the silver gauge face thingies off) Roger did the top of the dash where the windshield met the dash- with no problems whatsoever. Had to get that crevice b/w windshield and dash with a paintbrush but you can't even tell. Looks real good so far, except it isnt all put back together yet, I drove home with only the dash and door panels in.<BR>Even if there had been some errors it wouldnt not have mattered one bit, since I have new carpet and am completely repainting the car another color.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A><P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>Tarheels Fieros Website</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||William||02-24-2001||11:17 PM||||Be sure and post some pics! I too have repainted the interior. My dash and consoles were painted black and everything else was covered in tan leather. I just installed new carpet today, and it looks like this Huge project may actually be done tommorow. After spending close to $1500 on the interior and well over 100 hours in time, I'm dying to post some pics myself!||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroLisa||02-25-2001||12:06 AM||||Well I took some pics today while I was working on it, but my camera ran out of batterys about 30 seconds ago so I dont know if my pics will be ruined since I have to put new ones in. But I will have pics sometime soon- mine is flat black with a semi gloss gray...I can't wait till its all put together/||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||02-25-2001||12:01 PM||||ya left ur bagel...........lol<P>I was afraid of that by where the back nuts were. We should be able to sheer off the plastic studs with the tool I showed you, and just bond the new one on. Prob wont hurt the old one, just wont have the mounting studs anymore. BTW howd the 'shift' lite work.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 02-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroLisa||02-25-2001||03:11 PM||||Roger- hm I forgot to pay attention to the shift light, I was too busy being blinded by those dang lightbulbs in the center console... By the way, I went to the barn today and opened the doors and they still look good, didnt get scratched at all w/ door closing.<BR>And I remembered I forgot my bagel earlier this morning when I was craving one. Oh well.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||CHOWITT31||02-26-2001||06:06 PM||||Greetings from Delaware Lisa.<BR>It is possible to remove the map pocket with the dash in place I just installed a new one on my 85.<BR>However the top left mount can not be reached without removal of the dash.<BR>you can reach the top right if you remove the dash speaker.<BR>The 2-bottom mounts I was able to reach by loosening 2-lower dash mounts on the passenger side and pulling it forward about an inch.<BR>When I removed mine I broke off the top left mount, so when I installed the new one I just cut off the top left mount and secured the area with 2-sided tape.<BR>It is very secure due to the backing of the map pocket being so stiff.<BR>Hope this helps<BR>See Ya<BR>Ken||||reg||6
